current_fingerprint (read side, raw file reads that may degrade to a gate miss) and published_fingerprint (publish side, every leg falling back to a sentinel) must derive the same five canonical inputs — HEAD oid, head tree oid, .git/index checksum, wikiignore hash, worktree signature — in byte-identical form, because a generation is keyed by their digest: any divergence makes the gate miss forever and republish on every invocation, with no type or test tying the two derivations together. The sentinel values are the load-bearing difference, not an inconsistency: an unborn HEAD, a missing .git/index, and an absent .wikiignore must still publish a generation.
